["Which statement about evolution is correct?","populations evolve over generations; individuals do not evolve by choice during their lives","individuals evolve whenever they need to","evolution always moves species toward perfection","Evolution is a change in a population's inherited traits over generations, driven by processes such as selection, not a choice or a goal."],
["Why are specialist species generally at greater risk than generalists when habitats change rapidly?","specialists depend on narrow conditions or resources that may disappear, while generalists can use alternatives","specialists have more genetic diversity","generalists cannot survive in any changed habitat","A specialist with one food or habitat has few options if it vanishes, whereas generalists can switch resources."]
